            <ArticleTitle>Insights into the interplay between electric fields and microstructures of AEL films under ionothermal conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1836-1839</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10021j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A facile method for precise microstructure control of molecular sieve films remains a great challenge. In contrast to conventional hydrothermal methods, herein AEL molecular sieve films with preferred c-orientation are in situ fabricated through elaborate programming of the applied electric fields under ionothermal conditions. The approach developed here may pave a new avenue for designing and fabricating high quality molecular sieve films with diverse microstructures and functionality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
